> limit log(z) z -> -1
  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)
limit of log(z) as z -> -1:
  does not exist: the values along different directions differ
    along arg(z - a) = 0: pi*i
    along arg(z - a) = pi/4: pi*i
    along arg(z - a) = pi/2: pi*i
    along arg(z - a) = 3pi/4: pi*i
    along arg(z - a) = pi: pi*i
    along arg(z - a) = -3pi/4: -pi*i
    along arg(z - a) = -pi/2: -pi*i
    along arg(z - a) = -pi/4: -pi*i
> limit sqrt(z) z -> -1
  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)
limit of sqrt(z) as z -> -1:
  does not exist: the values along different directions differ
    along arg(z - a) = 0: i
    along arg(z - a) = pi/4: i
    along arg(z - a) = pi/2: i
    along arg(z - a) = 3pi/4: i
    along arg(z - a) = pi: i
    along arg(z - a) = -3pi/4: -i
    along arg(z - a) = -pi/2: -i
    along arg(z - a) = -pi/4: -i
> limit log(z) z -> 1
  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)
limit of log(z) as z -> 1:
  = 0
  checked numerically along 8 directions (arg(z - a) = 0, pi/4, ..., -pi/4), z -> a by factors of 4: all agree
  log(z) is continuous there: f(1) = 0
> complex log(z^2)
  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)
  note: z = x + iy (real and imaginary parts real)
  note: i is the imaginary unit; x, y are taken as real
log((x + i*y)^2) = log(x^4 + 2x^2*y^2 + y^4)/2 + i*atan2(2x*y, x^2 - y^2)
  Re = log(x^4 + 2x^2*y^2 + y^4)/2,  Im = atan2(2x*y, x^2 - y^2)
  check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 2e-16)
> complex sqrt(z^2)
  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)
  note: z = x + iy (real and imaginary parts real)
  note: i is the imaginary unit; x, y are taken as real
sqrt((x + i*y)^2) = sqrt((x^2 - y^2 + sqrt(x^4 + 2x^2*y^2 + y^4))/2) + i*copysign(sqrt((y^2 - x^2 + sqrt(x^4 + 2x^2*y^2 + y^4))/2), 2x*y)
  Re = sqrt((x^2 - y^2 + sqrt(x^4 + 2x^2*y^2 + y^4))/2),  Im = copysign(sqrt((y^2 - x^2 + sqrt(x^4 + 2x^2*y^2 + y^4))/2), 2x*y)
  check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 7e-16)
> complex re(log(z))
  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)
  note: z = x + iy (real and imaginary parts real)
  note: i is the imaginary unit; x, y are taken as real
re(log(x + i*y)) = log(x^2 + y^2)/2
  Re = log(x^2 + y^2)/2,  Im = 0
  check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 2e-16)
> complex im(log(z))
  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)
  note: z = x + iy (real and imaginary parts real)
  note: i is the imaginary unit; x, y are taken as real
im(log(x + i*y)) = atan2(y, x)
  Re = atan2(y, x),  Im = 0
  check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points
> complex re(sqrt(z))
  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)
  note: z = x + iy (real and imaginary parts real)
  note: i is the imaginary unit; x, y are taken as real
re(sqrt(x + i*y)) = sqrt((x + sqrt(x^2 + y^2))/2)
  Re = sqrt((x + sqrt(x^2 + y^2))/2),  Im = 0
  check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 2e-16)
> complex im(sqrt(z))
  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)
  note: z = x + iy (real and imaginary parts real)
  note: i is the imaginary unit; x, y are taken as real
im(sqrt(x + i*y)) = copysign(sqrt((sqrt(x^2 + y^2) - x)/2), y)
  Re = copysign(sqrt((sqrt(x^2 + y^2) - x)/2), y),  Im = 0
  check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 1e-15)
> complex log((-1)^2)
log((-1)^2) = 0
  Re = 0,  Im = 0
  check: equal numerically (0, complex arithmetic)
> complex sqrt((-1)^2)
sqrt((-1)^2) = 1
  Re = 1,  Im = 0
  check: equal numerically (1, complex arithmetic)
> complex log(-1)^(1/2)
log(-1)^(1/2) = 1.253314137 + i*1.253314137
  Re = 1.253314137,  Im = 1.253314137
  check: equal numerically (1.253314137 + 1.253314137i, complex arithmetic)
> complex exp(2*log(z))
  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)
  note: z = x + iy (real and imaginary parts real)
  note: i is the imaginary unit; x, y are taken as real
exp(2log(x + i*y)) = cos(2atan2(y, x))*exp(log(x^2 + y^2)) + i*sin(2atan2(y, x))*exp(log(x^2 + y^2))
  Re = cos(2atan2(y, x))*exp(log(x^2 + y^2)),  Im = sin(2atan2(y, x))*exp(log(x^2 + y^2))
  check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 7e-16)
> complex log(exp(z))
  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)
  note: z = x + iy (real and imaginary parts real)
  note: i is the imaginary unit; x, y are taken as real
log(exp(x + i*y)) = log(exp(x)^2)/2 + i*atan2(exp(x)*sin(y), exp(x)*cos(y))
  Re = log(exp(x)^2)/2,  Im = atan2(exp(x)*sin(y), exp(x)*cos(y))
  check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 2e-16)
